From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:59:43 +0100
Subject: dt-bindings: soc: qcom: pmic-glink: Add qcom,no-battery

On boards with no battery the firmware battery manager still reports one
as present, so the battery client exposes a power supply with meaningless
values. Document a boolean that lets such boards skip the battery client
while keeping the USB Type-C and alternate mode clients.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml
@@ -65,6 +65,12 @@ properties:
       The array should contain a gpio entry for each PMIC Glink connector, in reg order.
       It is defined that GPIO active level means "CC2" or Reversed/Flipped orientation.
 
+  qcom,no-battery:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      No battery is fitted. Skip the battery manager client, which would
+      otherwise expose a battery that the firmware always reports as present.
+
   nvmem-cells:
     minItems: 3
     maxItems: 3
-- 
